From 011555816cabebad3b21b6d43d81c26a4781f4b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@localhost>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:03:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 19/21] Transform feedback captured by geometry shaders

Transform feedback was a stub: the bound buffer was recorded but never bound to any shader
stage, Begin/End only toggled a flag, counter buffers were ignored, and geometry shaders with
transform feedback did not compile (DXVK stream output, zink with its geometry shader on every
draw).

- Geometry shaders (mesh emulation) capture transform feedback through SPIRV-Cross's mesh
  stream, to up to 4 buffers. MoltenVK allocates the buffers, session state, per-primitive
  slots and mode as implicit buffers of the geometry stage.
- vkCmdBindTransformFeedbackBuffersEXT records the buffers per binding (offsets and sizes).
- vkCmdBeginTransformFeedbackEXT creates the session state: bound sizes, and byte offsets
  starting at 0 or, with counter buffers, at the counter values (copied on the GPU).
  vkCmdEndTransformFeedbackEXT writes the byte offsets reached to the counter buffers.
- A direct draw with transform feedback active and a capturing geometry shader runs a pass
  counting the captured vertices of each input primitive, a compute pass turning the counts into
  vertex slots in primitive order (primitives that do not fit in a buffer are not written, the
  offsets advance by the vertices written), and the drawing pass writing the vertices at their
  slots. Indirect draws do not capture (logged).
- Vertex and tessellation evaluation shaders with transform feedback (no geometry shader) fail
  pipeline creation with VK_ERROR_FEATURE_NOT_PRESENT instead of writing to an unbound buffer.
- Transform feedback properties: 1 stream, 4 buffers, no queries, no vkCmdDrawIndirectByteCountEXT.
